# 14. Guiding Principles

Every architectural decision should

- Preserve backward compatibility where practical
- Prioritize security and privacy
- Be metadata-driven before code-driven
- Favor reusable services over duplication
- Keep AI explainable and governed
- Support multi-tenancy from day one
- Remain cloud-neutral where feasible

---

# 15. Risks & Mitigations

| Risk | Mitigation |
|------|------------|
| AI model changes | Provider abstraction and evaluation framework |
| Vendor lock-in | Open standards and pluggable architecture |
| Regulatory changes | Metadata-driven policies and governance |
| Performance growth | Horizontal scaling and event-driven architecture |
| Customer customization | Extension framework and marketplace |

